outputs.exact_statement:
For every integer $n\ge2$, every nontrivial increasing family $\mathcal P$ of graphs on $n$ vertices invariant under all vertex permutations, and every $0<\varepsilon<1/2$, $$\label{eq:threshold}
 p_{1-\varepsilon}(\mathcal P)-p_\varepsilon(\mathcal P)
 \le \frac{2^{19}}{(\log n)^2}\log\frac1{2\varepsilon}.$$

Let $F\subseteq E_n$, put $H=E_n\setminus F$, and, for $y\in\{0,1\}^{H}$, let $f_y(x)=f(x,y)$ for $x\in\{0,1\}^{F}$. If $y$ has the Bernoulli-$p$ product law, then, for every real $k>0$, $$\begin{aligned}
 \mathbb E_y\sum_{\substack{A\subseteq F\\1\le |A|\le k}}
        \widehat{f_y}(A)^2
 &=\sum_{\substack{S\subseteq E_n\\1\le|S\cap F|\le k}}
        \widehat f(S)^2,
 \label{eq:restriction-mass}\\
 \mathbb E_y I(f_y)&=\sum_{e\in F}I_e(f).
 \label{eq:restriction-influence}
\end{aligned}$$

